meta {
  name: WatchDemand (stream)
  type: grpc
  seq: 3
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.DemandService/WatchDemand
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "demand_id": "dem-1"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  Server-side streaming: the stage ruler, messages and findings in real time.

  The BFF subscribes to this stream and converts it into SSE for the browser —
  real time is a projection of the event log, not polling (ADR-0006).
}
